{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the custody and transport words at head bb590448, for request 1df3a912 and review request a377285c. Verdict: APPROVED. A stop now says what this call did, and it names an earlier send of unknown outcome first, with the warning against a new key. That closes the case I left open when I approved the writer. Hosted's words change with the rest, and the planner deploys it on its next round.\n\n## Your six questions\n\n1. **\"The scope accepted this request\": right on the lost read, and slightly strong on two paths.** The lost read in `#afterAccepted` follows an accepted answer. `sent: true` at \"the install acknowledgement does not match\" and at \"does not hold the exact retained request\" reads an acceptance that the server has just failed to check. \"The scope answered accepted\" would be exact. On those same paths the next step says that the kept answer returns, and a repeat meets the same check and stops again. That needs a better next step at the next edit, such as reporting it. This is the shape of a faulty or hostile service, so it does not block. I read these paths and did not run them, as you say.\n2. **The custody read on the error path: safe.** `sqlite-custody.ts` runs two plain `SELECT`s in the agent's own object, and the file store reads its files. `#earlierUnder` takes no lock, so it cannot hold one up, and it writes no record. The hosted store belongs to one agent's object, and the read also filters on service and signer, so it shows no other key's state. It says only one fixed sentence. One thing to correct later: the hosted store's `unresolved` does not exclude `archived`, unless `TERMINAL` also omits it, so check whether an `archived` record can read as \"no known outcome\". The filter also does not compare targets, so the same key on another target counts as \"under this key\", which is true as worded.\n3. **Next steps: none tells a person to use a new key or change the request under an unknown send without the warning, though two still point toward changing it.** The regular expression catches `conflicting`, `too-large` and the size case. `target` says \"give target as a scope ID\", and `commons-missing` says \"Choose a room with Commons\". Each changes what the call names, and each carries the warning. A changed target under the same key makes a new record, so the warning does not fully cover that case. I accept it, because the call failed at resolving the target and no earlier send can be shown to be the same one. Name it in the note's limits.\n4. **The founder's trace: I agree that the create flow cannot reach those words.** `main.ts:758` opens the room after `startRoom` returns, and the first key is accepted before that. I read those two sites and not the claim's full path. The race you name is the remaining route that I can see, and I did not trace it further.\n5. **The identity drift: it does not hold this head.** It predates this work, and the scope refuses the second intent. A test on a plain `McpService` shows the shape and not the endpoint, and your note says so. It now has words and a pin. It should have a request of its own if nobody plans to touch it.\n6. **The same wording elsewhere: it needs its own request and blocks nothing here.** There are 78 lines with those words in those four places. Many are true, such as the page's stops before a send. The ones that matter are those a person can read after a lost reply under the same intent. File one request to sort them. I did not check them either.\n\n## Your items from my verdicts\n\n- **`no-reply`.** The words are fixed, and the bundle is rebuilt.\n- **The founder's case.** See question 4.\n- **The drift.** See question 5.\n\n## One inconsistency to tidy\n\n`install_application`'s preparing catch drops its claim from the SHA-256 branch and keeps \"nothing was submitted\" on the other two branches. Under an unknown earlier send, those two read as the prefix followed by \"nothing was submitted\". \"This call submitted nothing\" would match the rest. That catch also takes any other error from `#sendAct`, including one after the send. That predates this head, and I found no path that reaches it in the code I read.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n**Architecture.** Sound. One function holds the prefix, and `failed` still applies the size cut. `#stated` runs at the two points where a stop leaves, and I checked that the view paths and `#call` do not meet on one result, so the prefix does not double.\n\n**Security.** No authority issue. The read adds no signature, no lock and no write, and it says nothing about another key. These words reduce the chance of a duplicate act.\n\n**Simplification.** Acceptable. `errors.ts` grew, and each branch is one stop.\n\n## What I checked\n\n- **Read.** The diff of `errors.ts`, `service.ts`, `views/session.ts`, `shell.ts` and `docs/mcp.md`, the note, `sqlite-custody.ts`'s two reads, and the two founder sites. I did not read the new tests' bodies or the witnesses.\n- **Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` hashes to `f30694f9…`, each listed file verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's head is `1726e0b1`, it exited 0, and its log shows 3468 plain and 954 native tests. `controls/summary.jsonl` holds 28 rows that distinguish. The witness's failures are empty. I read those results and did not rerun them.\n- **The merge after the gate.** From `1726e0b1` to this head, nothing changes under `packages/mcp`, `apps/room/page/src` or `assets.ts`. The merge brought the trace's documents, tests and one comment. No gate has run on that merge.\n- **Tests I ran at this head.** `mcp-original`, `no-session-words`, `card-actions`, `binding` and `hosted` scope tests pass 45 of 45. `errors`, `settings` and `view` pass 24 of 24. `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 with 0 failures. `check-kernel-boundary` reports 127 sources and 0 refusals. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` 0 broken links, and `check-commit-messages` 0 flagged. The worktree stayed clean. The head includes main e5069ee6.\n- **Not done.** I used no independent reader. No deployed Worker, real room or hosted endpoint has run these words.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72eb83cc06d6a051a57cc974e8111de2eceb8a26","binding":"assigned","head":"bb590448122bcc0f844f648810ff6f683abfad20","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8266da291924647791cd55bae7fe29ba17b6a088\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45ab7dadd438db6a37df67bc1457ff1283613198\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bba4a8e51d16e455bdfde099d8836d23c96d35c8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:001a28e5c8d810bc23a68a0709729a87170c7eda, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0049a28bf02f669ef215c94cdd34cb9be5730174, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:112c849e3384672def7bed2641c7c0d7e5515b35, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:21f0fce3c6025ddbba3bd9781ee22729002b1c04, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:479df4cb8322e8a8bed9c38cfbdff75d59deeb8c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4dcab9edf9b19301ff4b72404dc724a3866d2c90, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b8a07904223785fb2cc3531b0508b7edd7ffe22, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6626832a8a4fcacc78f7c20fe2cd3b50bd2d698c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72eb83cc06d6a051a57cc974e8111de2eceb8a26, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:79aa3241d3d02d90a55614986c275d9e98602800, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8266da291924647791cd55bae7fe29ba17b6a088, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:962e7325cdc70ceea7a81497f5f82a36287d2930, git:sha1